Language Takeaway

28
00:01:30,990 --> 00:01:33,790
Okay, so everyone's heard of a lamp, a light.

29
00:01:34,490 --> 00:01:38,970
This is something that you use to read in the dark, for example, to see in the dark.

30
00:01:39,240 --> 00:01:43,240
But in this case we have a floor lamp.

31
00:01:43,240 --> 00:01:45,050
So this is a lamp you put on the floor.

32
00:01:45,430 --> 00:01:46,090
Yes, exactly.

33
00:01:46,640 --> 00:01:49,760
So usually this lamp would be a lot taller.

34
00:01:49,760 --> 00:01:52,750
It'll maybe be like a meter taller, a meter and a half maybe.

35
00:01:53,250 --> 00:02:00,090
Okay, so for example, in your living room next to your sofa, you might have a very tall floor lamp.

36
00:02:00,410 --> 00:02:02,330
This allows you to get more light in the room.

37
00:02:02,650 --> 00:02:05,870
Right, so sometimes you know the center light in your living room is not enough.

38
00:02:06,150 --> 00:02:09,270
You want maybe more light in the corners, you get a little floor lamp.

39
00:02:09,840 --> 00:02:11,990
Okay, so that's the first item.

40
00:02:12,840 --> 00:02:16,230
Now that we go to the bedroom, we are getting an armoire.

41
00:02:16,750 --> 00:02:17,930
Okay, an armoire.

42
00:02:18,590 --> 00:02:19,930
This is kind of like a wardrobe.

43
00:02:20,410 --> 00:02:25,750
It's a piece of furniture we use to keep clothes in, but usually they're hanging clothes.

44
00:02:26,310 --> 00:02:30,600
Okay, so a closet is usually inside a wall, right?

45
00:02:30,920 --> 00:02:33,000
Right, so a closet's a part of your house.

46
00:02:33,440 --> 00:02:33,940
It's not furniture.

47
00:02:34,520 --> 00:02:40,420
Right, so an armoire is the same as a closet, but it's not in the house, like in the walls.

48
00:02:40,680 --> 00:02:41,000
It's outside.

49
00:02:41,300 --> 00:02:42,020
It's a piece of furniture.

50
00:02:42,280 --> 00:02:42,800
It's a big box.

51
00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:44,800
Yeah, I could pick it up and move it.

52
00:02:44,800 --> 00:02:45,800
Okay.

53
00:02:45,800 --> 00:02:47,960
Yes, so an armoire is a tall place to keep clothing.

54
00:02:47,960 --> 00:02:49,160
Usually you hang your clothes.

55
00:02:49,520 --> 00:02:51,500
You hang your shirts and your dresses and your coats.

56
00:02:52,640 --> 00:02:54,650
And moving on, we have a dresser.

57
00:02:55,080 --> 00:02:56,600
Now this seems pretty straightforward.

58
00:02:56,600 --> 00:02:58,070
To get dressed, you have a dresser.

59
00:02:58,390 --> 00:03:03,030
Yeah, it makes a lot of sense, but there is a big difference here between an armoire and a dresser.

60
00:03:03,170 --> 00:03:05,610
A dresser is usually drawers.

61
00:03:06,330 --> 00:03:10,670
So you keep your sweaters, your shirts, your socks, your underwear in a dresser.

62
00:03:10,870 --> 00:03:15,650
Okay, so an armoire, as you said, usually you hang your shirts or your pants.

63
00:03:16,490 --> 00:03:17,650
It's for hanging stuff only.

64
00:03:18,290 --> 00:03:23,890
A dresser is you have different drawers where you can put your socks, your boxer shorts, and any other things that you keep.

65
00:03:24,090 --> 00:03:24,410
Exactly.

66
00:03:24,910 --> 00:03:26,110
Okay, very good.

67
00:03:26,290 --> 00:03:30,530
So two very handy words, and that's what makes the difference between a closet.

68
00:03:30,880 --> 00:03:32,880
So many people say, oh, it's just a closet.

69
00:03:32,880 --> 00:03:33,880
Well, a closet's different.

70
00:03:34,010 --> 00:03:35,990
No, a closet is actually part of your house.

71
00:03:36,190 --> 00:03:37,510
It's a part of the wall.

72
00:03:37,840 --> 00:03:38,840
Maybe it has a door.

73
00:03:38,840 --> 00:03:41,800
Yeah, there's a big difference there.

74
00:03:41,800 --> 00:03:42,800
Okay.

75
00:03:42,800 --> 00:03:48,490
So moving on, we have a nightstand that's also usually in the bedroom.

76
00:03:49,320 --> 00:03:50,320
That's right.

77
00:03:50,320 --> 00:03:53,070
So I always wondered, why is it called a nightstand and not a daystand?

78
00:03:54,010 --> 00:03:55,550
Well, a nightstand, it makes sense.

79
00:03:55,720 --> 00:03:58,370
It usually has a lamp on it, a light on it.

80
00:03:58,840 --> 00:04:06,120
And so when you're in bed and you want to read, you have a nightstand next to you to put your lamp so you can turn the lamp on.

81
00:04:06,120 --> 00:04:07,290
Usually I also keep my books here.

82
00:04:07,770 --> 00:04:10,150
So when I'm reading, I put my books down, then I go to sleep.

83
00:04:10,750 --> 00:04:14,050
Some people also keep their glasses and their alarm clock on a nightstand.

84
00:04:14,590 --> 00:04:16,870
It's a small table that stands next to your bed.

85
00:04:17,170 --> 00:04:17,710
Very good.

86
00:04:18,560 --> 00:04:21,910
And our last word for language takeaway part one, we have a coffee table.

87
00:04:22,280 --> 00:04:22,590
Okay.

88
00:04:22,630 --> 00:04:25,830
So with the coffee table, Marco, we're moving back into the living room.

89
00:04:26,430 --> 00:04:29,030
And in the living room, you have a sofa, you have some chairs.

90
00:04:29,590 --> 00:04:31,790
You need a table, but you don't want a big table.

91
00:04:31,970 --> 00:04:35,310
You want a small table or a very short table.

92
00:04:35,960 --> 00:04:38,160
This is a coffee table.

93
00:04:38,160 --> 00:04:39,430
It's called a coffee table.

94
00:04:40,110 --> 00:04:41,210
I'm not really sure why.

95
00:04:41,310 --> 00:04:44,860
I guess because if you're having coffee in the living room, this is where you put the coffee.

96
00:04:45,080 --> 00:04:45,440
That's right.

97
00:04:45,600 --> 00:04:47,740
And we even have something called coffee table books.

98
00:04:48,040 --> 00:04:54,420
These are big, beautiful books, hardback books that have many pictures that you put on your coffee table to look nice.

99
00:04:55,820 --> 00:04:57,880
It's not for you to actually read all the time.

100
00:04:57,880 --> 00:05:02,640
Well, I read them, but it's more important to use these books to look nice.

101
00:05:03,400 --> 00:05:07,920
This is interesting though, because in many other countries, they're not really called a coffee table.

102
00:05:08,280 --> 00:05:12,440
A direct translation wouldn't really help you in many cases.

103
00:05:12,440 --> 00:05:15,100
I think in Chinese, it's called a tea table, not a coffee table.

104
00:05:15,480 --> 00:05:16,480
It makes sense.

105
00:05:16,480 --> 00:05:17,480
Right?

106
00:05:17,480 --> 00:05:20,720
I know in Spanish, it's just called a center table.

107
00:05:20,720 --> 00:05:21,720
Okay.

108
00:05:21,720 --> 00:05:30,600
So this is basically the low table you have in your living room next to your sofa, in front of your sofa actually, so you can have tea or coffee and read books.

109
00:05:30,600 --> 00:05:31,880
Or put your feet up while you're watching TV.

110
00:05:32,240 --> 00:05:34,160
Not in my house when I was a kid.

111
00:05:35,040 --> 00:05:36,040
All right.

112
