131
00:06:29,640 --> 00:06:29,980
Language Takeaway

132
00:06:32,280 --> 00:06:36,020
Coming up, we have one of my favorite phrases in the English language.

133
00:06:36,400 --> 00:06:40,020
I don't know why I like it so much, but it is a great name for a piece of furniture.

134
00:06:40,640 --> 00:06:41,640
A loveseat.

135
00:06:41,640 --> 00:06:42,640
Loveseat.

136
00:06:42,640 --> 00:06:42,900
Okay.

137
00:06:43,640 --> 00:06:44,640
Okay.

138
00:06:44,640 --> 00:06:45,440
It sounds very romantic.

139
00:06:45,740 --> 00:06:45,980
It does.

140
00:06:46,640 --> 00:06:47,640
A loveseat.

141
00:06:47,640 --> 00:06:48,640
Well, think about a sofa.

142
00:06:48,640 --> 00:06:49,000
A sofa can be very large.

143
00:06:49,640 --> 00:06:51,560
You can have four or five people on a sofa.

144
00:06:51,560 --> 00:06:52,560
Right.

145
00:06:52,560 --> 00:06:54,520
But a loveseat is a small sofa for two people.

146
00:06:54,880 --> 00:06:55,100
Okay.

147
00:06:55,880 --> 00:06:56,680
So that's what makes the difference, right?

148
00:06:57,080 --> 00:07:00,280
It's a sofa, but only two people can sit on this.

149
00:07:00,680 --> 00:07:01,680
That's right.

150
00:07:01,680 --> 00:07:03,680
So a sofa, it's not a loveseat.

151
00:07:03,680 --> 00:07:11,260
And what about if it's one, because usually sofa sets, you have a loveseat, a big one, and you have one, sometimes an individual one.

152
00:07:11,440 --> 00:07:12,640
Do you just call that a chair?

153
00:07:12,920 --> 00:07:13,920
Yep.

154
00:07:13,920 --> 00:07:14,920
A chair.

155
00:07:14,920 --> 00:07:15,920
A chair.

156
00:07:15,920 --> 00:07:16,920
Okay.

157
00:07:16,920 --> 00:07:17,920
Exactly.

158
00:07:17,920 --> 00:07:18,920
We'll come to it in a minute.

159
00:07:18,920 --> 00:07:21,040
There's a special kind of chair that it might be, but we're not quite there yet.

160
00:07:21,040 --> 00:07:26,600
First, we have another kind of chair, which is very special and reminds me a lot of the 1970s.

161
00:07:27,280 --> 00:07:27,600
Right.

162
00:07:27,780 --> 00:07:33,000
We have a bean bag, and this is actually a piece of furniture that's still very popular in many places.

163
00:07:33,420 --> 00:07:40,480
And it's called a bean bag because it's a huge bag that is filled with beans.

164
00:07:40,940 --> 00:07:41,240
Right.

165
00:07:41,240 --> 00:07:42,580
Beans or something soft.

166
00:07:43,320 --> 00:07:48,640
And when you sit on it, it looks like a ball, but when you sit on it, it can change shape.

167
00:07:48,900 --> 00:07:49,060
Right.

168
00:07:49,680 --> 00:07:51,600
It molds to what shape you are.

169
00:07:52,240 --> 00:07:53,060
And usually they're very light.

170
00:07:53,480 --> 00:07:58,820
A lot of times, I hate to say it, a lot of times bachelors' apartments have these.

171
00:08:00,480 --> 00:08:00,650
That's right.

172
00:08:01,480 --> 00:08:04,110
It's actually a very cheap piece of furniture, and it's comfortable.

173
00:08:04,680 --> 00:08:07,930
Sometimes if you're watching TV, you can just sit on your bean bag and watch TV.

174
00:08:08,400 --> 00:08:15,720
Even I know some people may fall asleep on a bean bag as guests.

175
00:08:15,720 --> 00:08:19,820
I've never slept on, well, maybe once, but I don't remember sleeping on a bean bag.

176
00:08:19,920 --> 00:08:21,440
I imagine it's quite uncomfortable.

177
00:08:21,440 --> 00:08:22,840
Yeah, for your back.

178
00:08:22,840 --> 00:08:31,080
But moving on after a bean bag, which is a good informal piece of furniture, we have a dining set, which is a lot nicer.

179
00:08:31,340 --> 00:08:32,220
Okay, dining set.

180
00:08:32,560 --> 00:08:33,560
All right.

181
00:08:33,560 --> 00:08:35,520
So a dining set has many pieces.

182
00:08:35,520 --> 00:08:37,000
You have a dining room table.

183
00:08:37,180 --> 00:08:37,480
Right.

184
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:39,340
And you have chairs.

185
00:08:39,340 --> 00:08:43,800
So a set is basically a collection of a table and chairs together.

186
00:08:43,800 --> 00:08:52,520
Sometimes I think it will also include some type of piece of furniture that's next to the dining table where you can keep your plates and you can keep your teacups and all that.

187
00:08:52,860 --> 00:08:53,280
What's that called?

188
00:08:53,520 --> 00:08:54,360
That's called a buffet.

189
00:08:55,480 --> 00:08:58,920
And that's basically, it's like a dresser for your dining room.

190
00:08:58,920 --> 00:08:59,410
Right, exactly.

191
00:08:59,920 --> 00:09:05,270
It's got like drawers and stuff for your plates, your cups, like you said, and it's next to the dining room table.

192
00:09:06,200 --> 00:09:10,600
But the dining room set or the dining set is for the dining room.

193
00:09:10,600 --> 00:09:11,730
It's the table where you eat dinner.

194
00:09:12,160 --> 00:09:13,070
Okay, very good.

195
00:09:13,880 --> 00:09:17,330
And now moving on to that special chair that I am a big fan of.

196
00:09:18,340 --> 00:09:21,370
It's very comfortable to sit on and it's called a recliner.

197
00:09:23,070 --> 00:09:24,910
So we have a word here, recline.

198
00:09:25,080 --> 00:09:30,200
It means to lie back, to put your head back, to get comfortable.

199
00:09:30,200 --> 00:09:37,840
So a recliner is a chair that you can change the shape of to make you lie down flat.

200
00:09:38,360 --> 00:09:41,800
So when you sit down, you're sitting, but what if you want to lie down in a chair?

201
00:09:42,080 --> 00:09:43,120
This chair lets you do that.

202
00:09:43,580 --> 00:09:53,260
And it also, from the bottom part where your feet are, a little thing pops up so you can rest your feet on top of this little extension of the chair.

203
00:09:53,640 --> 00:09:56,240
Okay, so it has a built-in footrest.

204
00:09:56,320 --> 00:09:58,060
Footrest, exactly.

205
00:09:58,060 --> 00:09:59,140
So it's very comfortable.

206
00:09:59,140 --> 00:09:59,920
It's very popular.

207
00:10:00,340 --> 00:10:04,440
If you ever watch the series Friends, they have the recliners.

208
00:10:04,680 --> 00:10:06,500
It's very comfortable to watch sports, for example.

209
00:10:06,760 --> 00:10:07,760
You have your beer.

210
00:10:07,760 --> 00:10:08,540
Joey has his recliner.

211
00:10:08,760 --> 00:10:14,200
And remember when Joey and Chandler lived together, they have the two recliners in front of the TV.

212
00:10:14,200 --> 00:10:17,480
Those chairs are recliners and they're very, very popular.

213
00:10:17,480 --> 00:10:22,940
Actually I think in the United States, they're very commonly known by the brand, Lazy Boy.

214
00:10:23,640 --> 00:10:23,780
That's right.

215
00:10:24,640 --> 00:10:25,640
There's a brand.

216
00:10:25,640 --> 00:10:27,160
It's not a kind of furniture, but it's the name of the brand.

217
00:10:27,440 --> 00:10:29,280
It's Lazy Boy and they're very, very famous.

218
00:10:29,440 --> 00:10:32,080
You're right, Marco, for their reclining chairs.

219
00:10:32,080 --> 00:10:33,080
Exactly.

220
00:10:33,080 --> 00:10:37,880
So Lazy Boys, you may hear it, but the real word for it is called a recliner.

221
00:10:38,760 --> 00:10:40,640
So a lot of interesting pieces of furniture there.

222
