Okay, this is a great verb.

247
00:11:52,560 --> 00:11:53,130
To drop off.

248
00:11:53,800 --> 00:11:54,530
It's a verbal phrase.

249
00:11:55,390 --> 00:11:57,530
So the preposition there is off, not on.

250
00:11:58,680 --> 00:12:06,120
So I could say, for example, Marco, I'm just going to drop off my bag at home and then I'll meet you guys for dinner.

251
00:12:06,120 --> 00:12:09,390
That means I'm going to go to my house and put down my bag and then I'll leave.

252
00:12:09,960 --> 00:12:16,090
So to drop off is basically to go somewhere so you can put something in that place.

253
00:12:17,070 --> 00:12:19,430
But it doesn't mean that you're going to go to that place and stay there.

254
00:12:20,290 --> 00:12:27,290
So if I say, I'm going to drop off the kids at school, that means I'm going to take the kids and leave them at school and then go away.

255
00:12:27,490 --> 00:12:28,870
It doesn't mean you're going to school yourself.

256
00:12:30,110 --> 00:12:33,690
So can you drop off the laundry at the dry cleaners, please?

257
00:12:33,990 --> 00:12:34,430
Very good.

258
00:12:35,200 --> 00:12:37,970
So drop off the laundry to the dry cleaners, leave it there and then go somewhere else.

259
00:12:38,360 --> 00:12:40,870
So what happens at three o'clock when the kids are still at school?

260
00:12:41,560 --> 00:12:42,560
That's right.

261
00:12:42,560 --> 00:12:44,970
Now we use the opposite verbal phrase and that is to pick up.

262
00:12:45,320 --> 00:12:48,120
Okay, drop off, pick up.

263
00:12:48,120 --> 00:12:49,270
So you go pick up the kids.

264
00:12:49,700 --> 00:12:50,770
You go pick up the laundry.

265
00:12:51,560 --> 00:12:55,950
So this isn't just about picking something up from a table or the ground.

266
00:12:56,520 --> 00:12:58,550
You can actually use your car to pick something up.

267
00:12:58,760 --> 00:12:59,760
Right.

268
00:12:59,760 --> 00:13:00,840
You go and retrieve it.

269
00:13:00,840 --> 00:13:03,810
So I'm going to the post office to pick up my package.

270
00:13:05,120 --> 00:13:05,410
Very good.

271
00:13:06,120 --> 00:13:11,400
So phrases that you're going to have to use if you're talking about furniture, if you're talking about buying something.

272
00:13:11,400 --> 00:13:18,310
And while we're on the topic, I know that one of the most popular places to buy furniture is Ikea.

273
00:13:18,390 --> 00:13:19,350
Are you a big fan of Ikea?

274
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:24,310
I like Ikea and I love what they've done for people who don't want to spend too much money on furniture.

275
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:25,270
Furniture is expensive.

276
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:26,710
Furniture is very expensive.

277
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:29,560
You can spend $5,000 on a sofa.

278
00:13:29,560 --> 00:13:37,520
And so Ikea is a wonderful brand and I think a wonderful company because it makes good-looking furniture affordable.

279
00:13:37,520 --> 00:13:39,770
And it's because you put it together yourself, right?

280
00:13:40,190 --> 00:13:40,430
That's right.

281
00:13:40,840 --> 00:13:44,880
A lot of things you have to assemble or put together by yourself.

282
00:13:44,890 --> 00:13:47,290
So you buy it in a box and then you make it.

283
00:13:47,810 --> 00:13:55,270
It's a little bit frustrating sometimes, but for people like me, and I'm sure people like you, part of the fun is putting stuff together.

284
00:13:55,570 --> 00:14:00,390
Yeah, because you kind of feel like you kind of built it, but you really didn't.

285
00:14:00,550 --> 00:14:02,750
So it kind of gives you that false sense of accomplishment.

286
00:14:03,170 --> 00:14:06,110
It's like I'm in the 19th century and I can make my own furniture.

287
00:14:07,170 --> 00:14:09,510
So it's very popular.

288
00:14:11,600 --> 00:14:15,540
And apart from having great furniture, I understand that they have amazing meatballs.

289
00:14:15,920 --> 00:14:16,220
They do.

290
00:14:16,920 --> 00:14:18,720
Well, I'm a Swedish.

291
00:14:18,820 --> 00:14:20,180
I never get to eat Swedish meatballs.

292
00:14:20,820 --> 00:14:24,320
And here in China, they do have some of the better meatballs around.

293
00:14:25,180 --> 00:14:28,020
So I would recommend if you haven't tried them, try them.

294
00:14:28,280 --> 00:14:29,340
They're pretty good.

295
00:14:29,520 --> 00:14:30,520
Yeah, go to IKEA.

296
00:14:30,520 --> 00:14:31,440
Go to IKEA, have some dinner.

297
00:14:32,520 --> 00:14:32,840
Let me know.

298
00:14:33,520 --> 00:14:34,640
Our website is EnglishPod.com.

299
00:14:34,640 --> 00:14:36,480
Do you like IKEA and do you love their meatballs?

300
00:14:36,800 --> 00:14:37,140
All right.

301
00:14:37,600 --> 00:14:37,960
We'll see you guys there.

302
00:14:38,600 --> 00:14:39,600
Bye.

303
